From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: FE-VM/ehash chain bring-up (T-M6 FE-VM)

Consolidates the "FE-VM / ehash / FE chain" bring-up series (originally
labeled as one arc in this file's own section comment) into a single
patch: 0122 (fe-ehash-init), 0123 (fe-port-support), 0124
(fe-vm-singletons), 0125 (fe-ehash-table), 0126 (muram-genpool), 0127
(fe-vm-enq-root), 0128 (fe-vm-flow-insert), 0129 (offload-engage), 0130
(fe-ehash-dma-coherent), 0131 (fe-hash-object), 0132 (fe-arm-debugfs),
0133 (fe-arm-real-accc).

These twelve patches were always one coherent build-out of the FE-VM
hash-object/ehash subsystem, applied in strict sequence with nothing
else interleaved. Content is unchanged from their union, verified
against the real CI checkpoint commits in the persistent kernel-git-cache
(run 34558658476, checkpoints 2e1cf0adb202 "applied: 0121..." to
da9256c8e6be "applied: 0133..."), round-trip verified byte-identical via
both `patch -p1` and `git apply --3way`, and confirmed by re-running the
entire 122-patch reduced series from pristine v6.18.48 locally with zero
failures before this was ever pushed to CI.

Touches: fman_keygen.c, fman_pcd.c, fman_pcd_kg.c, fman_port.{c,h},
include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h.

Signed-off-by: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
